//! Symmetry generators for the PTM orientation fundamental zones.
//!
//! GENERATED FILE -- do not edit by hand. Regenerate with:
//!
//! ```text
//! python3 tools/gen_ptm_quat_tables.py \
//!     --source <upstream>/ptm_quat.cpp \
//!     --out crates/rmda-core/src/analysis/ptm/quat_tables.rs
//! ```
//!
//! `rotate_quaternion_into_fundamental_zone` selects the generator
//! with the largest `|q . g|` and rotates `q` by it, so each table's
//! length is exactly the order of the corresponding point group.
//!
//! Entries are exact decimals rather than the surd expressions upstream
//! writes, because `f64::sqrt` is not `const` and a Rust `const` cannot
//! call it. The upstream expression is kept as a trailing comment on
//! every element, and `tools/gen_ptm_quat_tables.py --check` asserts both
//! that the comment round-trips and that the decimal is bit-identical to
//! what C++ computes.
//!
//! DCUB reduces over [`CUBIC`]; DHEX and GRAPHENE over the order-12
//! conventional set [`HCP_CONVENTIONAL`].
#![allow(clippy::approx_constant)]

